[{:present #{["M-aif-a-matrix-faithfulness" :pattern-done ["problems/r3-belief-update" 6]]}, :absent #{}}]}, :produces #{["M-aif-a-matrix-faithfulness" :pattern-done ["translation/choose-the-equivalence-check" 8]]}, :theta 1/2, :theta-record {:status :no-recorded-trials, :unattributed-rows 0}}}}}, :arrangement {:nodes [{:pattern-rationale "The mission goal is explicitly a faithful belief-update observation model.", :fragment-span {:start 11, :end 62}, :occurrence-id ["problems/r3-belief-update" 0], :roles ["goal"], :source-sha256 "51d9459b4ec25cf4c63b98a72a10c45847471ea44c4804ff2da06fe394254c70", :sentence-id "s1", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "problems/r3-belief-update", :objects {:G {:text "    The census (library-loop L1) found only six problem-stating nodes for 1256 patterns, so most @why edges had nothing to land on; minting the dossier problems as nodes is the recorded-corpus repair.\n    + evidence: futon2 holes labs wm-contract PROBLEMS-r1-r3-r3a-batch3.md, section \"## R3 — Belief update\", subsection \"The problem it solves\".", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r3-belief-update.flexiarg", :sha256 "51d9459b4ec25cf4c63b98a72a10c45847471ea44c4804ff2da06fe394254c70"}, :situation-source "pinned pattern BECAUSE part and citation rationale", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "reason to apply: The mission goal is explicitly a faithful belief-update observation model."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    A pattern's rationale is that it answers the problem this node states.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r3-belief-update.flexiarg", :sha256 "51d9459b4ec25cf4c63b98a72a10c45847471ea44c4804ff2da06fe394254c70"}, :situation-source "pinned target-reading fragment", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "observed fragment: Make the belief-update observation model A faithful"}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The problem, verbatim from the dossier: R3 solves how observations change belief without either overwriting it or letting it become immovable: the roster places **“Belief update”** in BELIEVE (`p4ng/empirics-futon/control-stages.edn:18`; control-stage numbering). The operational contract requires prediction error, precision weighting, variational free energy, and an update step all to be computed by name (`docs/futon-aif-completeness.md:80-106`; contract R3). The catalogue prescribes moving belief toward observation only as far as learning rate and channel trust allow, while **“never letting that uncertainty fall below a floor”** (`p4ng/sec-catalog.tex:198`; catalogue R3). The registry writes the reduction as `mu <- mu + alpha Pi eps`, importing prior belief, precision, error, and step size (`holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:104-107`; control-stage R3). R3 therefore solves controlled revision: the direction comes from error, the amount from learning rate and trust, and retained uncertainty prevents false certainty. (source: futon2 holes labs wm-contract PROBLEMS-r1-r3-r3a-batch3.md, R3, The problem it solves)\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r3-belief-update.flexiarg", :sha256 "51d9459b4ec25cf4c63b98a72a10c45847471ea44c4804ff2da06fe394254c70"}, :situation-source "pinned pattern HOWEVER part", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "pattern tension: problems/r3-belief-update"}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Treat this node as the landing point for @why edges from patterns that answer it; solving the problem itself is scoped by the dossier's residual-problems list, not by this node.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r3-belief-update.flexiarg", :sha256 "51d9459b4ec25cf4c63b98a72a10c45847471ea44c4804ff2da06fe394254c70"}, :situation-source "pinned pattern THEN/CHECK part", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "checked result for faithful-observation-model"}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [0], :pattern "problems/r3-belief-update"} {:pattern-rationale "The dated fragment supplies temporal context that must remain structured provenance.", :fragment-span {:start 104, :end 114}, :occurrence-id ["realtime/structured-events-only" 1], :roles ["context"], :source-sha256 "19708084425ea5d2f70f36e5603640b28062a74c1fc8ebdf5a8380db95fa5b28", :sentence-id "s2", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "realtime/structured-events-only", :objects {:G {:text "    Stable schema enables accurate parsing, dedupe, and audit trails.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/realtime/structured-events-only.flexiarg", :sha256 "19708084425ea5d2f70f36e5603640b28062a74c1fc8ebdf5a8380db95fa5b28"}, :situation-source "pinned pattern BECAUSE part and citation rationale", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "reason to apply: The dated fragment supplies temporal context that must remain structured provenance."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    PSR/PUR are emitted as free-text or inconsistent key names.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/realtime/structured-events-only.flexiarg", :sha256 "19708084425ea5d2f70f36e5603640b28062a74c1fc8ebdf5a8380db95fa5b28"}, :situation-source "pinned target-reading fragment", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "observed fragment: 2026-07-13"}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Humans may annotate context outside the structured event payload.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/realtime/structured-events-only.flexiarg", :sha256 "19708084425ea5d2f70f36e5603640b28062a74c1fc8ebdf5a8380db95fa5b28"}, :situation-source "pinned pattern HOWEVER part", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "pattern tension: realtime/structured-events-only"}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Emit PSR/PUR as structured event maps with :event, :pattern/id, :session/id, :decision/id; keep annotations in separate fields.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/realtime/structured-events-only.flexiarg", :sha256 "19708084425ea5d2f70f36e5603640b28062a74c1fc8ebdf5a8380db95fa5b28"}, :situation-source "pinned pattern THEN/CHECK part", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "checked result for mission-dated"}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [1], :pattern "realtime/structured-events-only"} {:pattern-rationale "OPEN INSTANTIATE names an implementation phase whose absence would otherwise be hidden behind design artifacts.", :fragment-span {:start 129, :end 149}, :occurrence-id ["process/built-but-not-wired-invisibility" 2], :roles ["context"], :source-sha256 "c5eb3aafa23d07670d9ef1a56ac3f3746cc585ebfd515796bacc8e4630beac48", :sentence-id "s3", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "process/built-but-not-wired-invisibility", :objects {:G {:text "    Each instance is individually correct and the defect lives only in the wiring — no per-component test can catch it; only a rung that refuses on unconsumed machinery can.\n    + evidence: N-process-trap-recording-conventions.md section 1, T3, six receipts ([WM] x1 naming four instances, [APM] x5, incl. futon3c aa139dce). Authority grounding: WR-27, a loop is born instrumented for its gain — machinery outside the loop it instruments has no gain and no reality.", :source {:path "futon3/library/process/built-but-not-wired-invisibility.flexiarg", :sha256 "c5eb3aafa23d07670d9ef1a56ac3f3746cc585ebfd515796bacc8e4630beac48"}, :situation-source "pinned pattern BECAUSE part and citation rationale", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "reason to apply: OPEN INSTANTIATE names an implementation phase whose absence would otherwise be hidden behind design artifacts."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    A component exists, elaborates or runs, and nothing on its intended path calls it.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/process/built-but-not-wired-invisibility.flexiarg", :sha256 "c5eb3aafa23d07670d9ef1a56ac3f3746cc585ebfd515796bacc8e4630beac48"}, :situation-source "pinned target-reading fragment", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "observed fragment: OPEN — **INSTANTIATE"}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Binary accounting cannot represent inhabited-but-unconsumed, so it reads as present.\n    + VIOLATION (WM): four confirmed instances, including the R14 dial and fixture-fed EIG. Receipt: futon2 holes EPIC-run-era.md, via N-process-trap-recording-conventions.md T3.\n    + VIOLATION (APM): campaign_trace emit! and the Lean trace checker — the designated acceptance authority — wired only to the success path; frame_park_decisions/-main left unwired when the watcher's mutation path was correctly removed (futon3c aa139dce), caught only by cross-reading two individually-correct packets; process_watchdog/default-notify! shells out to notify-send, which is not installed on the host — a dead escalation path of unknown age; apm-axiom-audit.service runs beside the machine and was never a criterion inside it, which is what permitted T1's b00J02.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/process/built-but-not-wired-invisibility.flexiarg", :sha256 "c5eb3aafa23d07670d9ef1a56ac3f3746cc585ebfd515796bacc8e4630beac48"}, :situation-source "pinned pattern HOWEVER part", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "pattern tension: process/built-but-not-wired-invisibility"}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Treat consumption as a checked rung (the conventions note's rung grammar: constructed then wired, never skipping); wire the acceptance authority to failure paths as well as success; keep an inventory of unwired components so invisibility is a listed fact, not an archaeology result.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/process/built-but-not-wired-invisibility.flexiarg", :sha256 "c5eb3aafa23d07670d9ef1a56ac3f3746cc585ebfd515796bacc8e4630beac48"}, :situation-source "pinned pattern THEN/CHECK part", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "checked result for instantiate-phase-open"}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [2], :pattern "process/built-but-not-wired-invisibility"} {:pattern-rationale "The named sponsor plus unassigned implementer is a capability and ownership boundary.", :fragment-span {:start 256, :end 293}, :occurrence-id ["coordination/capability-gate" 3], :roles ["context"], :source-sha256 "1e606844bad799c1931c812b2f33e801ae4c3680bc792d7f441511eb8fc55a04", :sentence-id "s4", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "coordination/capability-gate", :objects {:G {:text "    otherwise failures are silent and attribution is unclear (who was supposed to do what?)", :source {:path "futon3/library/coordination/capability-gate.flexiarg", :sha256 "1e606844bad799c1931c812b2f33e801ae4c3680bc792d7f441511eb8fc55a04"}, :situation-source "pinned pattern BECAUSE part and citation rationale", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "reason to apply: The named sponsor plus unassigned implementer is a capability and ownership boundary."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    you want to route tasks to heterogeneous agents (humans, Codex, Claude, services)\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/coordination/capability-gate.flexiarg", :sha256 "1e606844bad799c1931c812b2f33e801ae4c3680bc792d7f441511eb8fc55a04"}, :situation-source "pinned target-reading fragment", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "observed fragment: Joe + unassigned implementation owner"}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    without authorization, tasks can be executed by agents that lack tools, permissions, or responsibility\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/coordination/capability-gate.flexiarg", :sha256 "1e606844bad799c1931c812b2f33e801ae4c3680bc792d7f441511eb8fc55a04"}, :situation-source "pinned pattern HOWEVER part", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "pattern tension: coordination/capability-gate"}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    require the agent to be present in the registry and validate capability match at G4\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/coordination/capability-gate.flexiarg", :sha256 "1e606844bad799c1931c812b2f33e801ae4c3680bc792d7f441511eb8fc55a04"}, :situation-source "pinned pattern THEN/CHECK part", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "checked result for owner-plus-unassigned-implementer"}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [3], :pattern "coordination/capability-gate"} {:pattern-rationale "The repository fragment identifies the authoritative implementation substrate.", :fragment-span {:start 314, :end 320}, :occurrence-id ["hygiene/observe-the-authority" 4], :roles ["context"], :source-sha256 "f43c2229b97e9162b4b62af0093f5d15854423b1fc810cd0da4ccdc5ed568bef", :sentence-id "s5", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "hygiene/observe-the-authority", :objects {:G {:text "    A verdict about state is only as current as the read behind it, and a stale read that passes is indistinguishable from a true pass.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hygiene/observe-the-authority.flexiarg", :sha256 "f43c2229b97e9162b4b62af0093f5d15854423b1fc810cd0da4ccdc5ed568bef"}, :situation-source "pinned pattern BECAUSE part and citation rationale", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "reason to apply: The repository fragment identifies the authoritative implementation substrate."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    A policy's decision depends on the state of something outside the process making the decision.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hygiene/observe-the-authority.flexiarg", :sha256 "f43c2229b97e9162b4b62af0093f5d15854423b1fc810cd0da4ccdc5ed568bef"}, :situation-source "pinned target-reading fragment", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "observed fragment: futon2"}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    A local stand-in is cheaper and usually right, and it is wrong silently: it drifts exactly when the thing it stands in for has moved.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/hygiene/observe-the-authority.flexiarg", :sha256 "f43c2229b97e9162b4b62af0093f5d15854423b1fc810cd0da4ccdc5ed568bef"}, :situation-source "pinned pattern