ned target-reading fragment", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "observed fragment: `M-aif-faithfulness` (parent badge audit)"}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Free-form handoff text drops structured evidence; reviewers cannot find a warrant they are not told about; and a warrant for yesterday's base is worse than none if it is trusted.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/test-registry/warrant-rides-the-handoff.flexiarg", :sha256 "c4a1c658f35f8bcb2eb5690c3af863dc8f69402f9ad29817960d5634c6979aba"}, :situation-source "pinned pattern HOWEVER part", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "pattern tension: test-registry/warrant-rides-the-handoff"}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Put base sha and warrant entry ids into the handoff's structured fields; type the handoff :warranted or :unwarranted; have the reviewer's reply return its review entry id.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/test-registry/warrant-rides-the-handoff.flexiarg", :sha256 "c4a1c658f35f8bcb2eb5690c3af863dc8f69402f9ad29817960d5634c6979aba"}, :situation-source "pinned pattern THEN/CHECK part", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "checked result for cites-parent-badge-audit"}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [5], :pattern "test-registry/warrant-rides-the-handoff"} {:pattern-rationale "The cited R1/R3 wiring is directly about the belief-update mechanism this mission instantiates.", :fragment-span {:start 388, :end 417}, :occurrence-id ["problems/r3-belief-update" 6], :roles ["dependency"], :source-sha256 "51d9459b4ec25cf4c63b98a72a10c45847471ea44c4804ff2da06fe394254c70", :sentence-id "s7", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "problems/r3-belief-update", :objects {:G {:text "    The census (library-loop L1) found only six problem-stating nodes for 1256 patterns, so most @why edges had nothing to land on; minting the dossier problems as nodes is the recorded-corpus repair.\n    + evidence: futon2 holes labs wm-contract PROBLEMS-r1-r3-r3a-batch3.md, section \"## R3 — Belief update\", subsection \"The problem it solves\".", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r3-belief-update.flexiarg", :sha256 "51d9459b4ec25cf4c63b98a72a10c45847471ea44c4804ff2da06fe394254c70"}, :situation-source "pinned pattern BECAUSE part and citation rationale", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "reason to apply: The cited R1/R3 wiring is directly about the belief-update mechanism this mission instantiates."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    A pattern's rationale is that it answers the problem this node states.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r3-belief-update.flexiarg", :sha256 "51d9459b4ec25cf4c63b98a72a10c45847471ea44c4804ff2da06fe394254c70"}, :situation-source "pinned target-reading fragment", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "observed fragment: `M-aif-wiring` (R1/R3 wiring)"}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The problem, verbatim from the dossier: R3 solves how observations change belief without either overwriting it or letting it become immovable: the roster places **“Belief update”** in BELIEVE (`p4ng/empirics-futon/control-stages.edn:18`; control-stage numbering). The operational contract requires prediction error, precision weighting, variational free energy, and an update step all to be computed by name (`docs/futon-aif-completeness.md:80-106`; contract R3). The catalogue prescribes moving belief toward observation only as far as learning rate and channel trust allow, while **“never letting that uncertainty fall below a floor”** (`p4ng/sec-catalog.tex:198`; catalogue R3). The registry writes the reduction as `mu <- mu + alpha Pi eps`, importing prior belief, precision, error, and step size (`holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:104-107`; control-stage R3). R3 therefore solves controlled revision: the direction comes from error, the amount from learning rate and trust, and retained uncertainty prevents false certainty. (source: futon2 holes labs wm-contract PROBLEMS-r1-r3-r3a-batch3.md, R3, The problem it solves)\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r3-belief-update.flexiarg", :sha256 "51d9459b4ec25cf4c63b98a72a10c45847471ea44c4804ff2da06fe394254c70"}, :situation-source "pinned pattern HOWEVER part", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "pattern tension: problems/r3-belief-update"}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Treat this node as the landing point for @why edges from patterns that answer it; solving the problem itself is scoped by the dossier's residual-problems list, not by this node.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r3-belief-update.flexiarg", :sha256 "51d9459b4ec25cf4c63b98a72a10c45847471ea44c4804ff2da06fe394254c70"}, :situation-source "pinned pattern THEN/CHECK part", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "checked result for cites-aif-wiring"}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [6], :pattern "problems/r3-belief-update"} {:pattern-rationale "Formal fidelity and behavioural evidence are different verification relations and must be checked accordingly.", :fragment-span {:start 467, :end 508}, :occurrence-id ["translation/choose-the-equivalence-check" 8], :roles ["rationale"], :source-sha256 "9d07c643c2d6ea6a8404e94127a420d09067f98ece8495698d40be0f452f5e07", :sentence-id "s8", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "translation/choose-the-equivalence-check", :objects {:G {:text "    Each kind leaves a different kind of evidence behind.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/translation/choose-the-equivalence-check.flexiarg", :sha256 "9d07c643c2d6ea6a8404e94127a420d09067f98ece8495698d40be0f452f5e07"}, :situation-source "pinned pattern BECAUSE part and citation rationale", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "reason to apply: Formal fidelity and behavioural evidence are different verification relations and must be checked accordingly."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "   